3db9-2e9d-5ea4-a615-95b4e61aba9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102324" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]=-12+8=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]=16+6=22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 22\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89245d79-d07d-52fc-b200-d036359ea5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489830} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec329dc-1748-52dd-b167-d53c2b2de5f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489838} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb2be99-4d40-5ce0-8615-04e936d37155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489962} {:answer/id #uuid "d5cedc30-2694-5244-bfcb-f9f82cdcc31e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489988} {:answer/id #uuid "ede240b8-195a-5dc0-9427-2e395b73f909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5cedc30-2694-5244-bfcb-f9f82cdcc31e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489988} :answer-field/id #uuid "846614c1-9a14-59e2-9c4d-0efd9f8946b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f89c3382-117b-502e-8af6-ebca79b6f083" :question/math-academy-id "q-102354" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 2+8\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+8+8}{1+4+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot 3=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ecf8788-69f4-5834-812b-5702d49e4f4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348862} {:answer/id #uuid "7038e2ce-8c22-56c7-bce9-4531c5d29eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349480} {:answer/id #uuid "741b3734-968c-5909-903f-3a1aadd10955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349513} {:answer/id #uuid "ad057dc2-b49e-5c5b-8cd2-a865922a7c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349981} {:answer/id #uuid "df7ddcb6-3b2b-5373-bd11-799c6429dd8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad057dc2-b49e-5c5b-8cd2-a865922a7c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349981} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b38458-09c8-5aec-b568-d48ebb9481a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0ea9087-dcb2-563d-a61a-22e857198678" :question/math-academy-id "q-81103" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $15{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot (-3)}{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+12}{1+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n15{x}_{1}=15\\cdot \\frac{7}{5}=21.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2297f5c1-de21-5ae7-bdaa-c11eef2db9ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489594} {:answer/id #uuid "2323e7de-6036-569e-953d-d977998ad9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489596} {:answer/id #uuid "5620e6f6-75a0-5f4a-8f11-1f0be3b41912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489716} {:answer/id #uuid "98d031cb-9e96-593d-bd25-1d64d893572e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489855} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f0d473-5189-54a8-aa7b-ef8f87c0b58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6f0d473-5189-54a8-aa7b-ef8f87c0b58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489915} :answer-field/id #uuid "81c27db6-a846-5a45-83a3-5a70d18bec75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d4f28f0-6e57-5f1c-b187-80e59b881c47" :question/math-academy-id "q-81108" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $2{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{41}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{41}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{41}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{41}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{41} \\\\ -9 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{41}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{41} \\\\ -9 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{41}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{41}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{41}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-15+0-8 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}=2\\cdot (-23)=-46.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35584b0d-5f36-530c-95c4-8d8dec57a042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489635} {:answer/id #uuid "62645a61-af8c-50c1-891a-ec2a1bd6ffa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489746} {:answer/id #uuid "a7dfba1c-89fc-5799-a7ce-902a9097fb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489885} {:answer/id #uuid "b077d275-d97e-5b1d-b7c1-156af5d3749c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489901} {:answer/id #uuid "cf87e655-37bd-5819-8214-e0383ae42a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35584b0d-5f36-530c-95c4-8d8dec57a042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489635} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f22f005-276f-5d7e-8ec0-5d5973524d87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbba5a71-4786-5f34-9118-2344153343aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-81140" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}=3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
